# Kotlin style

- Kotlin official style + ktlint. 4-space indent. No wildcard imports.
- Prefer `val`, data classes, and exhaustive `when`. Avoid `Any` and unchecked casts.
- Public `:core` APIs get KDoc. Internal implementation stays `internal` unless a test in another package needs it.
- Domain types (`PetState`, `CareEvent`, `EvolutionBranch`) live in `:core`. Room `*Entity` types live in `:app`.
- Do not put simulation math in Compose, ViewModels, Workers, or DAOs.
- Coroutines for async. No `GlobalScope`. ViewModel/UseCase owners use `viewModelScope` or an injected scope.
- Errors: fail loud in `:core` with typed results or exceptions that `:app` maps to UI. Never swallow.

```kotlin
// BAD — math in UI
Button(onClick = { pet.hunger = (pet.hunger - 2).coerceAtLeast(0) })

// GOOD — UI dispatches, core computes
Button(onClick = { viewModel.onFeed() })
```
